<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/10th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fatimid conquest of Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/969">969 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as bloodless conquest of Egypt</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fatimid conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in 969 CE was led by the general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jawhar-al-siqilli">Jawhar al-Siqilli</a>, who took the country with little resistance from the weakened Ikhshidid regime. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> then founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a> as its new capital, making Egypt the centre of its power.</p></div>
